│ patch_name               │ multi_start_greedy_with_local_search                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current code runs a single greedy pass with random sampling, so the result varies a   │
│                          │ lot and often gets stuck in a bad local ordering. Two improvements: (1) run many greedy   │
│                          │ restarts with different random starting transactions and keep the best schedule found,    │
│                          │ and (2) add a cheap local search (adjacent-swap improvement) on the best schedule to      │
│                          │ squeeze out further makespan reductions. Since greedy construction is fast (only          │
│                          │ ~num_samples cost evaluations per step), doing many restarts is affordable and directly   │
│                          │ improves expected makespan. The swap-based local search exploits the fact that swapping   │
│                          │ two adjacent transactions in the sequence only changes conflict-induced delays locally,   │
│                          │ so small perturbations can yield meaningful makespan reductions. We keep the original     │
│                          │ greedy as a fallback structure but wrap it in a restart loop and polish with local        │
│                          │ search.                                                                                   │
