│ patch_name               │ modular_multistart_insertion_search                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver into a pipeline of modular components: (1) a conflict-graph        │
│                          │ analysis to compute per-transaction conflict footprints, (2) a multi-start greedy         │
│                          │ constructor that uses lookahead sampling over full candidate evaluation, and (3) a hybrid │
│                          │ local-search refiner combining adjacent-swap, random-swap, and segment-reinsertion moves  │
│                          │ under a unified time budget. The architecture separates construction from refinement and  │
│                          │ alternates between them (GRASP-like) so time is spent wherever improvement is found,      │
│                          │ which yields lower makespans than pure greedy restarts followed by a single hill-climb    │
│                          │ pass.                                                                                     │
