│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ annealing_insertion_search                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of greedy construction + 2-opt swaps, I use simulated annealing over full         │
│                          │ permutations with mixed move operators (adjacent swaps, block reversals, and reinsertion  │
│                          │ moves). Reinsertion moves are far more effective than pure swaps for sequencing problems  │
│                          │ because they can move a conflicting transaction across many positions at once. The        │
│                          │ annealing starts from the best of a few greedy constructions (warm start) and uses a      │
│                          │ geometric cooling schedule with restart-to-best on improvement, giving a fundamentally    │
│                          │ different search paradigm: stochastic hill-climbing over the whole solution space rather  │
│                          │ than deterministic local descent, which escapes local minima that trap the current 2-opt  │
│                          │ approach.                                                                                 │
