                        Patch Metadata - Gen 12/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ better_local_search_with_perturbation                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Reasoning step-by-step:                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current program spends ~25s on randomized greedy restarts, then runs a single      │
│                          │ adjacent-swap hill-climb until a local optimum (which restarts from scratch only when     │
│                          │ `improved` is False it just stops entirely — actually the while loop exits once no        │
│                          │ improving adjacent swap exists).                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Key weaknesses:                                                                        │
│                          │    - Adjacent swaps only explore a tiny neighborhood. Insertion moves (move a txn to a    │
│                          │ distant position) can escape local optima that swaps cannot.                              │
│                          │    - The hill climb is purely deterministic after finding a local optimum — it never      │
│                          │ perturbs to escape, so it gets stuck quickly.                                             │
│                          │    - It always restarts greedy from a fully random state; once a good solution exists,    │
│                          │ budget is better spent refining it.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Improvements:                                                                          │
│                          │    - Allocate a shorter construction phase (greedy restarts), keeping the best solution   │
│                          │ as a strong starting point.                                                               │
│                          │    - Add an Iterated Local Search (ILS): repeatedly perturb the best solution with a few  │
│                          │ random moves (random swaps/segment reversal), then hill-climb with a richer neighborhood  │
│                          │ (adjacent swap + random-pair swap + insertion), accepting only improvements. This is a    │
│                          │ well-known, effective metaheuristic for permutation scheduling problems like this one     │
│                          │ (makespan minimization over transaction orderings).                                       │
│                          │    - Keep checking the deadline so the function always terminates in time.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. This should reduce makespan further because ILS with insertion neighborhood escapes    │
│                          │ local optima that plain adjacent-swap descent cannot, while still exploiting the strong   │
│                          │ greedy solutions already found.                                                           │
