│ patch_name               │ or_opt_local_search                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Adjacent swaps can only fix local ordering issues; many suboptimal schedules have a small │
│                          │ block of 1–3 transactions that belongs elsewhere. Adding an Or-opt pass (remove a segment │
│                          │ of length 1–3 and try reinserting it at every other position), alternating with           │
│                          │ adjacent-swap hill climbing, explores a much richer neighborhood while staying within the │
│                          │ time budget. Each candidate is evaluated exactly via `get_opt_seq_cost`, so improvements  │
│                          │ always reflect the true makespan. This should reduce makespan further and raise the       │
│                          │ combined score.                                                                           │
