│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ in_place_two_opt_search                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search only performs adjacent swaps, which gets stuck in poor local     │
│                          │ minima quickly. A 2-opt style local search with in-place apply/undo of segment reversals  │
│                          │ explores a much larger neighborhood of orderings at low constant overhead (no full        │
│                          │ candidate list copies), enabling more improvement rounds within the same time budget. We  │
│                          │ replace the adjacent-swap local search with an in-place pairwise-swap (2-opt) search and  │
│                          │ apply it to every greedy restart's result (keeping the best), rather than only the single │
│                          │ best greedy schedule. This combines stronger local optimization with more diverse         │
│                          │ starting points, directly lowering makespan.                                              │
