│ patch_description        │ The current multi-restart greedy plus 2-opt reaches a strong local optimum but can get    │
│                          │ stuck since 2-opt only accepts strictly improving moves. I add a simulated annealing      │
│                          │ refinement stage entirely inside the evolve block: it starts from the 2-opt solution,     │
│                          │ proposes random adjacent/pair swaps, and accepts worsening moves with probability         │
│                          │ exp(-Δ/T) at a low temperature that decays geometrically — mostly downhill but able to    │
│                          │ escape 2-opt local optima. It tracks the global best, so it never returns worse than the  │
│                          │ 2-opt result. All needed imports (math, time) are done inside the function to avoid       │
│                          │ touching the immutable header.                                                            │
