│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shuffled_best_restarts                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters of the current approach: fixed 30 greedy restarts with sample_rate=0.9 and │
│                          │ 8 samples, followed by a full local search (swap + Or-opt). This ignores wall-clock       │
│                          │ budget — 30 restarts may underuse time. New configuration: (1) time-budgeted restart loop │
│                          │ (~8s deadline per workload), alternating between fresh randomized greedy constructions    │
│                          │ and, every 3rd restart, a perturbed copy of the current best ("shuffled best": remove 4–6 │
│                          │ random transactions, greedy reinsert each at its cheapest evaluated position). This keeps │
│                          │ the cost-guided greedy signal while starting restarts near a proven-good solution. (2)    │
│                          │ Apply local search to each candidate before comparing, so improved solutions seed         │
│                          │ subsequent perturbations. (3) Cheaper perturbation restarts also free time for more local │
│                          │ search passes on the incumbent.                                                           │
