╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_start_and_or_opt_moves                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Reasoning:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. The current algorithm uses a single greedy construction + local search +               │
│                          │ ruin-and-recreate. A known weakness of single-seed iterated local search is premature     │
│                          │ convergence to one basin. Keeping a small pool of diverse seeds (from multiple randomized │
│                          │ greedy constructions) and running ruin-and-recreate + local search on each spreads the    │
│                          │ search across basins, which is standard practice in ILS/beam-style scheduling optimizers. │
│                          │ 2. The local search only uses single-txn relocation and swaps. Adding Or-opt moves        │
│                          │ (relocating short contiguous segments of 2–3 transactions) is a classic improvement for   │
│                          │ sequencing problems because good schedules often require moving small blocks of dependent │
│                          │ transactions together.                                                                    │
│                          │ 3. The ruin operator currently only removes one contiguous segment. Removing multiple     │
│                          │ random scattered transactions ("random ruin") diversifies differently than contiguous     │
│                          │ "radial ruin" and is known (Schneider et al., ruin-and-recreate literature) to escape     │
│                          │ different local optima.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Build a pool of 3 seeds via greedy+local-search, each with a time slice, then continue  │
│                          │ ILS from the best, periodically re-seeding perturbations from the second-best to explore  │
│                          │ a different basin.                                                                        │
│                          │ - Add Or-opt segment relocation moves to the local search.                                │
│                          │ - Perturbation randomly chooses between contiguous ruin and scattered random ruin.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should lower makespan by exploring more of the search space within the same time     │
│                          │ budget.                                                                                   │
