│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ils_perturb_recreate                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The prior results show that randomized-restart greedy + local search (current, 277)       │
│                          │ underperforms the iterated-local-search variant (254), which perturbs the incumbent best  │
│                          │ with ruin-and-recreate and re-polishes each candidate with a bounded local-search slice.  │
│                          │ The key reasons: (1) pure restarts waste budget re-running the expensive greedy           │
│                          │ construction, (2) perturbing the best solution concentrates search in promising basins,   │
│                          │ and (3) bounded local-search slices prevent one candidate from consuming the whole        │
│                          │ budget. I restore that ILS structure and additionally mix in occasional greedy restarts   │
│                          │ for diversification, and alternate perturbation move types (segment ruin-and-recreate,    │
│                          │ relocation, swap) so the incumbent keeps escaping different local optima. Every candidate │
│                          │ is polished with a time-sliced local search and accepted only on improvement of the       │
│                          │ global best.                                                                              │
