│ patch_description        │ The current program already uses greedy construction + iterated SA, but underperforms the │
│                          │ prior best (244 vs 256 makespan). Following the recommendation, I add Or-opt segment      │
│                          │ moves (extract a contiguous block of length 1–3 and reinsert it elsewhere) as a dedicated │
│                          │ move type in the SA neighborhood, alternating with single-transaction insertion moves.    │
│                          │ Segment reinsertions let the annealer relocate coherent chains of mutually-conflicting    │
│                          │ transactions at once, escaping local optima that single-element moves cannot. I also make │
│                          │ the acceptance phase slightly greedier (reheat kick threshold tightened) and reserve time │
│                          │ for a stronger final local-search polish. This richer neighborhood should recover and     │
│                          │ improve on the prior best makespan while keeping validity and schedule metrics unchanged. │
