│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ruin_and_recreate_sa_refine                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a ruin-and-recreate perturbation phase between the greedy restarts and the local      │
│                          │ search. After greedy construction produces a good base sequence, iteratively remove 3-8   │
│                          │ random transactions, then greedily reinsert each removed transaction (in random order) at │
│                          │ its best position evaluated with the true makespan cost. Accept only improvements and     │
│                          │ repeat until the time budget expires, keeping the best solution found. This combines the  │
│                          │ proven gain of ruin-and-recreate (23 makespan units at identical construction settings    │
│                          │ per Gen 20) with the existing descent, and effectively acts as a large-neighborhood       │
│                          │ search that escapes local optima that plain relocation/swap moves cannot.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
