│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lns_ruin_recreate_sa                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the greedy-restart-heavy approach with a Local Search / Large Neighborhood Search │
│                          │ pipeline: (1) build a small pool of initial solutions via randomized greedy construction, │
│                          │ (2) run a ruin-and-recreate LNS loop that removes a random 5-15% of transactions and      │
│                          │ greedily reinserts each at its best position (evaluated by real makespan), which jumps    │
│                          │ out of local optima far better than single-element moves, (3) polish with a               │
│                          │ low-temperature simulated annealing over insertion and adjacent-swap moves. All candidate │
│                          │ evaluations use the true makespan (get_opt_seq_cost), and the whole pipeline runs within  │
│                          │ a fixed time budget, restarting LNS from the incumbent whenever improvement stalls.       │
│                          │ Ruin-and-recreate perturbs many transactions at once while preserving good global         │
│                          │ structure, so it explores much more effectively than the previous greedy restarts, which  │
│                          │ discarded all structure each trial.                                                       │
