│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lns_destroy_repair_sa                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver around an Iterated Local Search / Large Neighborhood Search        │
│                          │ architecture with three clean phases: (1) randomized greedy construction, (2)             │
│                          │ destroy-and-repair perturbation starting from the incumbent best (every few trials,       │
│                          │ remove 4–6 transactions and greedily reinsert them at their cheapest positions), and (3)  │
│                          │ simulated annealing with mixed move neighborhoods and stagnation kicks. The               │
│                          │ destroy-repair moves operate near a proven-good basin instead of rebuilding from scratch, │
│                          │ giving cost-guided diversity that pure random restarts lack, while the modular phase      │
│                          │ structure keeps construction cheap so more improvement iterations fit in the time budget. │
